comment_data.body:
I've added some logging to see the response from the  language server. It turned out that completion candidates have the following structure (like for described above case):

<details><summary><code>textDocument/completion</code></summary>

```
{
  isIncomplete = true,
  items = { {
      command = {
        arguments = { 3 },
        command = "jetbrains.kotlin.completion.apply",
        title = "Apply Completion"
      },
      data = {
        configurationEntryId = "KotlinCompletionProvider"
      },
      kind = 3,
      label = "main",
      labelDetails = {
        description = "Unit",
        detail = "() (<root>)"
      },
      sortText = "0000000000",
      textEdit = {
        insert = {
          ["end"] = {
            character = 6,
            line = 2
          },
          start = {
            character = 6,
            line = 2
          }
        },
        newText = "",
        replace = {
          ["end"] = {
            character = 6,
            line = 2
          },
          start = {
            character = 6,
            line = 2
          }
        }
      }
    } }
}
```

</details>

<details><summary><code>completionItem/resolve</code></summary>

```
{
command = {
  arguments = { 3 },
  command = "jetbrains.kotlin.completion.apply",
  title = "Apply Completion"
},
data = {
  configurationEntryId = "KotlinCompletionProvider"
},
kind = 3,
label = "main",
labelDetails = {
  description = "Unit",
  detail = "() (<root>)"
},
sortText = "0000000000",
textEdit = {
  insert = {
    ["end"] = {
      character = 6,
      line = 2
    },
    start = {
      character = 6,
      line = 2
    }
  },
  newText = "",
  replace = {
    ["end"] = {
      character = 6,
      line = 2
    },
    start = {
      character = 6,
      line = 2
    }
  }
}
```

</details>

The problem lies in `textEdit.newText` being empty string. So 'mini.completion' here works as expected: it sees valid `textEdit` (since empty string is technically allowed here) and applies it when user accepts completion candidate. As new text is empty string and replaced region is empty, it looks like nothing happens.

I would say that 'mini.completion' does follow [LSP specification](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#completionItem) here. It also looks like a known issue of `kotlin-lsp`: Kotlin/kotlin-lsp#105.

It doesn't look proper for 'mini.completion' to universally fall back to `label` (and its range) if `textEdit.newText` is empty string. My hope was that you can adjust it by putting the following in the '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/kotlin.lua':

```lua
local process_kotlin_items = function(items, base)
  local res = MiniCompletion.default_process_items(items, base, { kind_priority = { Text = -1, Snippet = 99 } })
  for _, item in ipairs(res) do
    -- If `kotlin-lsp` returned "empty text edit", make it properly fall back to just using `label`
    -- https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlin-lsp/issues/105
    if (item.textEdit or {}).newText == '' then item.textEdit = nil end
  end
  return res
end

vim.b.minicompletion_config = { lsp_completion = { process_items = process_kotlin_items } }
```

Although it now inserts proper text, it doesn't *fully* falls back to as if LSP server returned correct result in the first place. The issue is rather technical. 'mini.completion' has to (as per design of 'omnifunc', see `:h complete-functions`) should first report column from where the completed base starts. It currently [does so before applying `config.lsp_completion.process_items`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/fb4ccfed03c1f0d9db702f93a65cb4c0c6c2832b/lua/mini/completion.lua#L451), so it computes it based on the raw server response. Like in the case of typing `ma` it computes it to be just at cursor (since `textEdit` said so), but it should be before `ma` (as per the `label`).

All problems would go away if one of the following happens:
1. The linked `kotlin-lsp` issue is resolved. For me it looks fairly clearly that this is not the behavior according to LSP spec. Neovim team [agrees here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/36621#issuecomment-3564812602).
2. 'mini.completion' applies `config.lsp_completion.process_items` *before* deciding the completion start column.

I'll take a look if 2 is feasible (but I am afraid it might not be), but I'd really encourage to somehow contribute to 1.
